"source_title":"Wellness Lounge | Cal Lutheran","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located on the Student Union's second floor in room 205B and accessible by elevator or stairs. Posted hours are Monday–Friday, 8 a.m.–5 p.m.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"the-den","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"The Den","title":"Choose a Lower-Sensory Place to Regroup","subtitle":"A private sensory-friendly room in the Student Union","notes":"Ask the Student Union Info Desk how to access the room, then use its soft lighting and weighted blankets for a quiet reset.","short_summary":"This intentionally low-sensory space supports rest and reflection, particularly for neurodiverse students and others seeking sensory relief.","evidence_claim":"The university lists The Den among Student Union amenities and describes it as a private, low-sensory space with weighted blankets, soft lighting, and calming visuals.","source_url":"https://www.callutheran.edu/student-life/student-union/amenities.html","source_title":"Amenities | Cal Lutheran","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official amenities page does not publish separate access hours or a room number; ask the Student Union Info Desk for current access details.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"seed-project-garden","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"SEEd Project Garden","title":"Trade Screen Time for a Garden Shift","subtitle":"Sustainable Edible Education space north of Hutton Field","notes":"Check the garden’s Instagram for current drop-in volunteer times, or contact the program to arrange a tour or student event.","short_summary":"A working campus garden functions as an outdoor classroom, living lab, volunteer site, and gathering place.","evidence_claim":"Cal Lutheran says the SEEd Project Garden is open for use by students and community members, hosts student-worker drop-in volunteer hours, and supports classes, research, tours, and events.","source_url":"https://www.callutheran.edu/students/garden/","source_title":"SEEd Project Garden | Cal Lutheran","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The garden is on north campus beyond Hutton Field. Volunteer days and times change and are announced through the garden's official Instagram account.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"kingsmen-park","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Kingsmen Park","title":"Take the Gathering Outside Under the Trees","subtitle":"Central-campus lawn divided by Kingsmen Creek","notes":"Use the shaded park as an event meetup point, and check the campus calendar or venue schedule before planning around a large gathering.","short_summary":"A central green space with shade trees and a creek accommodates a range of university outdoor events.","evidence_claim":"Cal Lutheran's venue page places Kingsmen Park in the center of campus and states that it is used for varied outdoor events, with Kingsmen Creek running between large shade-bearing trees.","source_url":"https://www.callutheran.edu/offices/campus-services/venue-detail.html?id=25","source_title":"Kingsmen Park | Venue Detail | Cal Lutheran","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor venue availability can change for scheduled events. Formal event bookings and associated charges are handled through Campus Services.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"alexander-twilight-lounge","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Alexander Twilight Legacy of Black Excellence Lounge","title":"Connect in a Space Shaped by Student Advocacy","subtitle":"Supportive community room inside the Student Union","notes":"Check the CCEI program calendar or email the center before visiting for a scheduled gathering, club meeting, or community program.","short_summary":"Black student advocacy helped establish this named lounge for connection, belonging, and community-building.","evidence_claim":"Cal Lutheran describes the Alexander Twilight Legacy of Black Excellence Lounge as an open, supportive community space serving Cal Lutheran's Black student community and credits Black Student Union and Sisters' Circle advocacy for its creation.","source_url":"https://www.callutheran.edu/students/cultural-engagement/ccei-spaces/alexandertwilight.html","source_title":"The Alexander Twilight Legacy of Black Excellence | Cal Lutheran","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located in the Student Union. Program schedules are maintained by CCEI; contact the center for current room access and event information.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ccei-patio","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"CCEI Patio","title":"Move a Club Conversation Into the Open Air","subtitle":"Student-created patio outside the Student Union’s upper level","notes":"Use the patio when no program is scheduled, or email CCEI ahead of time to request a reservation or accessibility support.","short_summary":"An outdoor gathering area created with student-government involvement gives culture and justice clubs room to meet and host programs.","evidence_claim":"Cal Lutheran states that the CCEI Patio was created with ASCLUG and student-life partners, is located outside the Student Union's upper level, and can be reserved by culture and justice clubs.","source_url":"https://www.callutheran.edu/students/cultural-engagement/ccei-spaces/cceipatio.html","source_title":"CCEI Patio | Cal Lutheran","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located outside the upper level of the Student Union near Mt. Clef Residence Hall. Email CCEI for reservations and accessibility requests.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
